{
 "about": "Per-weight prices (bits) of updated weights by role, measured on OLMoE-1B-7B-0924's published checkpoints (AdamW MoE), for benchmarks/nci/covering_priced.py --prices. Roles: qkv (attention q, k, v), attn_out (o), mlp_in / mlp_out = the ROUTED EXPERTS' gate+up / down (OLMoE's only MLPs; K2's routed experts read them), router, head, embed, norm (all measured), dense_mlp_in / dense_mlp_out = the dense-MLP equivalent (OLMoE attention x Pythia's MLP/attention ratio; K2's dense layer-0 MLP and shared expert, read by a loader that splits them, else they take mlp_in / mlp_out). Points olmoe@T: theta = step T, D = 5,000 steps (21B tokens), +10k: D = 10,000. Points pythia-P×olmoe@T: covering_priced's Pythia prices with the routed experts, router and norms at Pythia's attention price times OLMoE's measured ratio to attention at T; their cheapest tiers are Pythia's. cheapest: theta's forward-code classes over the block matrices (no Adam-v deciles: OLMoE publishes no optimizer state). Tiers by name: `theta 0.1%/1%/10%` are theta-selectable (theta's forward-code class over the block matrices; olmoe@T's 10% from the run's tables.md), `adam-v ...` also need theta's Adam-v decile (Pythia-160m's classes.out, selectable only with the optimizer state registered); `1%` and `0.1%` keep their first meaning (olmoe@T: theta's; the Pythia-anchored points: Pythia's code x Adam-v).",
 "caveats": "AdamW only: no Muon-trained MoE publishes intermediate checkpoints (Moonshot's Moonlight-16B-A3B, Kimi K2 and Kimi-Linear repos hold final weights only), so MuonClip is unmeasured; on a matched dense pair (300M Llama, deqing/convergent-llama-300M-{muon,adamw}-original, run r20261024-180717-a305) Muon's block matrices cost x1.11-1.14 / x1.19-1.35 / x1.39-1.65 AdamW's (bf16 / FP8 / FP4) and its MLP-to-attention ratio was 0.96 / 0.89-0.94 / 0.78-0.91. OLMoE's q and k are QK-normed and cost more than v and o; against v and o alone the routed experts cost x1.03-1.08 / x1.07-1.15 / x1.09-1.25, which puts the anchored points' K2 mean at x1.04-1.28 instead of x0.91-1.10 of the experts-at-dense-price mean. D = 5,000 steps (21B tokens) is OLMoE's finest spacing, against Pythia's 1,000 (2.1B tokens): absolute OLMoE prices are not Pythia's; the ratios held when D doubled (600k: D = 10,000). OLMoE publishes no fp32 master or Adam moments, so its prices use theta's bf16 codes only.",
